    <string name="close_notice">Close</string>
    <string name="data_notice_body">NilePay is operated by Premium Service. NilePay Merchant uses your merchant account to show payments and connect this device to your business.\n\nWith your consent and Android notification access, it processes supported InstaPay payment notifications in the background. Amount, sender handle, reference, timestamp, event and device identifiers, and app and Android versions are sent to the NilePay API over HTTPS for payment matching. Other apps’ notifications are ignored. Raw notification text is not stored or uploaded.\n\nParsed events wait in a local queue when delivery fails and are removed after successful delivery. Events older than seven days are discarded when the queue is processed; older entries may also be removed to keep the queue bounded. Authentication credentials are encrypted on this device. Server records are separate from the local queue.\n\nTo stop collection, disable NilePay notification access in Android settings or sign out. Signing out clears local credentials and consent; it does not delete your merchant account or existing server records. This app currently supports sign-in to an existing merchant account.\n\nPrivacy and support: nilepay.customers@gmail.com. Open the full policy for retention and provider details. To request deletion, use Settings → Delete account and verify your registered email. Public requests have a 72-hour cancellation period before daily cleanup removes or replaces personal fields. Limited pseudonymized payment records remain for the period stated in the full policy.</string>
